.It Xo
.Ic choose-buffer
.Op Fl NrZ
.Op Fl F Ar format
.Op Fl f Ar filter
.Op Fl O Ar sort-order
.Op Fl t Ar target-pane
.Op Ar template
.Xc
Put a pane into buffer mode: a list of the paste buffers with a preview of
the selected one.
Enter runs
.Ar template
with %% replaced by the buffer's name (default: paste it); p and P paste, d
and D delete, the selected buffer or the tagged ones.
The other keys and the flags are those of choose-tree; the sort orders are
creation, name and size.
.It Xo
.Ic choose-client
.Op Fl NrZ
.Op Fl F Ar format
.Op Fl f Ar filter
.Op Fl O Ar sort-order
.Op Fl t Ar target-pane
.Op Ar template
.Xc
Put a pane into client mode: a list of the attached clients.
Enter runs
.Ar template
(default: detach the client); d and D detach, x and X detach and hang up, z
and Z suspend.
The sort orders are name, size, creation and activity.
.It Xo
.Ic choose-tree
.Op Fl NrswZ
.Op Fl F Ar format
.Op Fl f Ar filter
.Op Fl O Ar sort-order
.Op Fl t Ar target-pane
.Op Ar template
.Xc
Put a pane into tree mode: sessions, their windows and their panes, one on
each line, with a preview of the selected one below.
-s starts with sessions collapsed, -w with windows collapsed, -Z zooms the
pane, -N starts without the preview, -f shows only the items a format is
true for, -O sets the sort order (index, name or activity) and -r reverses
it.
Enter, or the shortcut shown on a line, runs
.Ar template
with %% replaced by the target (default: switch to it).
Up, Down, PPage, NPage, Home and End move; Right and Left (or + and -)
expand and collapse; t tags, T untags all, C-t tags all; C-s searches and n
and N repeat; f asks for a filter and c clears it; O changes the sort
order and r reverses it; v toggles the preview; H returns to the starting
item; x kills the selected item and X the tagged ones after a y; : runs a
command for each tagged item; m marks the selected item's pane and M
clears the mark; S-Up and S-Down swap the selected window with the one
before or after it; C-h or F1 shows the keys; q leaves.
The command needs an attached client.
