.Ic send-keys Pq Ic send
.Op Fl FHlMRX
.Op Fl N Ar repeat-count
.Op Fl t Ar target-pane
.Oo Ar key Ar ... Oc
.Xc
Send keys to a pane. -l sends text literally, -H hexadecimal bytes, -N
repeats, -R resets the terminal, -X runs a copy-mode command, -F expands
formats.
Keys sent to a pane in copy mode go through the copy-mode key table, as if
typed.
-M, in a mouse key's commands, passes the mouse event to the pane's mode or
to its program if that asked for the mouse.
.It Xo
