Set a buffer's contents; -a appends, -n renames.
.It Xo
.Ic set-environment Pq Ic setenv
.Op Fl Fghru
.Op Fl t Ar target-session
.Ar variable Op Ar value
.Xc
Set a variable for the panes and shell commands started from now on in a
session, or in every session with -g. -r removes the variable from their
environment instead, -u forgets the entry, -h hides it (it is listed with
show-environment -h and not passed on), -F expands formats in the value.
.It Xo
.Ic set-hook
.Op Fl agpRuw
.Op Fl t Ar target-pane
.Ar hook Op Ar command
.Xc
Set the commands run when
.Ar hook
happens: for a session, with -g for all, and for the pane and window hooks
for a window or (-p) a pane. -a adds a command to the ones set, -u removes
them, -R runs the hook now.
.Ar hook
may be
.Ar name Ns Li \&[ Ns Ar index Ns Li \&]
to set or unset one command.
Hook names are those of
.Xr tmux 1 ;
the ones that run are listed in
.Pa docs/tmux-migration.md .
