.El
.Pp
Copy mode has the
.Li copy-mode
(emacs) and
.Li copy-mode-vi
tables, chosen by the
.Ic mode-keys
option; list them with
.Ic list-keys Fl T Ar table .
The mouse (on by default) selects panes and windows, resizes panes by their
borders, scrolls into copy mode and selects text (drag, or double and triple
click for a word and a line); the middle button pastes and the right one
opens a menu.
These are tmux's mouse keys in the root table
.Po Li MouseDown1Pane , WheelUpStatus , C-MouseDown3Border
and so on; list them with
.Ic list-keys Fl T Ar root Pc ,
and they are bound and unbound like other keys.
Once a pane is in copy mode the mouse there is not bound.
What the end of a selection does is the
.Ic mouse-drag-end
option: copy and leave copy mode (the default, as tmux), copy and stay, or
only select.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.It Ev LIF_SOCKET
Socket path used when neither
.Fl S
nor
.Fl L
is given and
.Ev LIF
is unset or empty.
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
If set, the default socket directory is
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lif .
.It Ev TMPDIR
Otherwise the socket directory is
.Pa $TMPDIR/lif- Ns Ar uid
.Pq Pa /tmp/lif- Ns Ar uid No without Ev TMPDIR .
.It Ev LIF_CONFIG
Configuration file to read instead of the default one.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
If set to an absolute path, the configuration file is
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lif/config.toml .
.It Ev HOME
Used for
.Pa ~/.config/lif/config.toml
and
.Pa ~/.tmux.conf .
.It Ev SHELL
The server's
.Ev SHELL
becomes the default for the
.Ic default-shell
option.
.It Ev VISUAL , Ev EDITOR
If the server's
.Ev VISUAL
(or else
.Ev EDITOR )
contains
.Ql vi ,
.Ic mode-keys
defaults to
.Ql vi .
.It Ev LIF
Set in every pane to
.Ar socket , Ns Ar server-pid , Ns Ar session-id .
Without
.Fl S
or
.Fl L ,
.Nm
uses the socket it names (before
.Ev LIF_SOCKET
and the default socket), so commands run in a pane reach that pane's
server.
.Nm
refuses to attach while it is set and not empty.
.It Ev LIF_PANE
Set in every pane to its pane id, for example
.Ql %3 .
.It Ev TMUX , Ev TMUX_PANE
Set in panes started while the
.Ic tmux-compat
option is on, like
.Ev LIF
and
.Ev LIF_PANE ,
for programs that only know
.Xr tmux 1 .
.El
.Pp
Programs in panes also get
.Ev TERM Ns = Ns Li xterm-256color ,
.Ev COLORTERM Ns = Ns Li truecolor ,
.Ev TERM_PROGRAM Ns = Ns Li lif
and
.Ev TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION ;
.Ev TMUX
(unless
.Ic tmux-compat
is on) and variables starting with
.Li TMUX ,
.Li LIF
or
.Li ZELLIJ
are not passed on from the client.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/lif/config.toml
The configuration file (TOML), unless
.Ev LIF_CONFIG
or
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
says otherwise.
Its settings are applied when the server starts and again by
.Ic source-file ;
the commands of its
.Li [startup]
section run once, when the server starts.
.It Pa $TMPDIR/lif- Ns Ar uid Ns Pa /default
The default socket.
The directory must be owned by the user with mode 0700.
.It Pa <socket>.lock
The server holds a lock on this file for as long as it runs; a client
that cannot connect but finds the lock held reports the server as not
responding instead of starting a second one.
The file stays when the server exits.
.El
.Sh SECURITY AND LIMITS
Only the user who started the server (and root) may connect to it; the
socket directory is mode 0700 and the socket 0600.
Of a client's environment only
.Ev COLORTERM , TERM_PROGRAM , TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION , SSH_AUTH_SOCK ,
.Ev SSH_CONNECTION , SSH_TTY , DISPLAY , WAYLAND_DISPLAY , LANG , LC_ALL ,
.Ev LC_CTYPE
and
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
reach new panes; the server drops anything else a client sends.
.Pp
While a client is attached the server reads keys from and draws on its
terminal itself, but only while the client is in the foreground of that
terminal: when a shell stops the client (job control, or SIGSTOP), what is
typed there goes to the shell and nothing is drawn over it.
A client stopped with SIGTSTP (or
.Ic suspend-client )
restores the terminal first.
.Pp
At most 1 MiB waits to be written to a pane's program.
A program that does not read its input gets nothing more once that much
waits: typed and pasted input is dropped with a message, terminal answers
and reports are dropped,
.Ic send-keys
and
.Ic paste-buffer
fail; the client's other keys keep working.
Other bounds: windows up to 10000 cells wide or high and 4 Mi cells in
all;
.Ic send-keys
at most 1 MiB of input per command and
.Fl N
at most 1000000; one format expands to at most 256 KiB;
.Ic source-file
reads regular files of at most 1 MiB;
.Ic { }
blocks nest at most 100 deep.
At most 64 shell commands
.Po
.Ic run-shell ,
.Ic if-shell ,
.Li #()
.Pc
run at once and 1 MiB of the output of each is kept; they are hung up when
the server exits.
At most 1024 command lists wait at a time (for a shell command or
.Ic wait-for ) .
Command output larger than one protocol frame is sent in parts.
The server raises its open-file limit to the hard limit (at most 65536)
and keeps 32 descriptors for clients when it creates panes; programs in
panes get the limit the server started with.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
In particular a command that fails (unknown target, invalid option,
unsupported command) exits 1, and
.Ic has-session
exits 1 when the session does not exist.
An attached client exits 0 when it is detached or its session ends.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start a named session, split it, and detach:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ lif new -s work
C-b %      (split side by side)
C-b d      (detach)
$ lif attach -t work
.Ed
.Pp
Print the panes of every session:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ lif list-panes -a -F '#{session_name}:#{window_index}.#{pane_index} #{pane_current_command}'
.Ed
.Pp
Convert a tmux configuration and check the result:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ lif migrate-tmux-conf > ~/.config/lif/config.toml
$ lif check-config
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tmux 1
.Pp
The documentation in the source tree:
.Pa README.md ,
.Pa docs/configuration.md ,
.Pa docs/copy-mode.md ,
.Pa docs/tmux-migration.md .
.Sh CAVEATS
The configuration file is TOML, not a list of tmux commands.
Scrollback is limited both by
.Ic history-limit
(lines, default 4000) and by
.Ic scrollback-bytes
(memory, default 10 MiB, allocated in whole pages so small budgets round
up); changing either applies to existing panes too.
Shell commands
.Po
.Ic run-shell ,
.Ic if-shell ,
.Li #() ,
.Ic copy-pipe
and the
.Ic copy-command
option
.Pc
run with
.Pa /bin/sh ,
not with
.Ic default-shell .
.Ic show-environment
lists only what
.Ic set-environment
set, and some hooks can be set but never run.
